","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"யா","tr":"yā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"தே","tr":"tē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"களரி","parts":[{"text":"களரி","lemma":"kaḷari","gloss":"saline wasteland"}],"gloss":"saline wasteland"},{"surface":"பரந்து","parts":[{"text":"பரந்து","lemma":"para","gloss":"having spread"}],"gloss":"having spread"},{"surface":"கள்ளி","parts":[{"text":"கள்ளி","lemma":"kaḷḷi","gloss":"spurge cactus"}],"gloss":"spurge cactus"},{"surface":"போகி","parts":[{"text":"போகி","lemma":"pō","gloss":"having grown high"}],"gloss":"having grown high"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பகலும்","parts":[{"text":"பகல்","lemma":"pakal","gloss":"daytime"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even in daytime"},{"surface":"கூஉம்","parts":[{"text":"கூஉம்","lemma":"kūvu","gloss":"hooting"}],"gloss":"hooting"},{"surface":"கூகையடு","parts":[{"text":"கூகையடு","lemma":"kūkai","gloss":"with the horned owl"}],"gloss":"with the horned owl"},{"surface":"பிறழ்","parts":[{"text":"பிறழ்","lemma":"piṟaḻ","gloss":"protruding"}],"gloss":"protruding"},{"surface":"பல்","parts":[{"text":"பல்","lemma":"pal","gloss":"tooth"}],"gloss":"teeth"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஈம","parts":[{"text":"ஈம","lemma":"īmam","gloss":"funeral pyre"}],"gloss":"funeral pyre"},{"surface":"விளக்கின்","parts":[{"text":"விளக்கின்","lemma":"viḷakku","gloss":"by the light of"}],"gloss":"by the light of"},{"surface":"பேஎய்","parts":[{"text":"பேஎய்","lemma":"pēy","gloss":"demoness"}],"gloss":"demoness"},{"surface":"மகளிரொடு","parts":[{"text":"மகளிரொடு","lemma":"makaḷir","gloss":"with women"}],"gloss":"with women"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அஞ்சுவந்","parts":[{"text":"அஞ்சுவந்","lemma":"அஞ்சுவந்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தன்று","parts":[{"text":"தன்று","lemma":"தன்று","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இம்","parts":[{"text":"இம்","lemma":"இம்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மஞ்சுபடு","parts":[{"text":"மஞ்சுபடு","lemma":"மஞ்சுபடு","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"முதுகாடு","parts":[{"text":"முதுகாடு","lemma":"முதுகாடு","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"நெஞ்சமர்","parts":[{"text":"நெஞ்சு","lemma":"neñcu","gloss":"heart"},{"text":"அமர்","lemma":"amar","gloss":"desiring"}],"gloss":"heart-desiring"},{"surface":"காதலர்","parts":[{"text":"காதலர்","lemma":"kātalar","gloss":"lovers"}],"gloss":"lovers"},{"surface":"அழுத","parts":[{"text":"அழுத","lemma":"aḻu","gloss":"wept"}],"gloss":"wept"},{"surface":"கண்ணீர்","parts":[{"text":"கண்ணீர்","lemma":"kaṇṇīr","gloss":"tears"}],"gloss":"tears"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"என்புபடு","parts":[{"text":"என்புபடு","lemma":"eṉpupaṭu","gloss":"bone-filled"}],"gloss":"bone-filled"},{"surface":"சுடலை","parts":[{"text":"சுடலை","lemma":"cuṭalai","gloss":"cremation ground"}],"gloss":"cremation ground"},{"surface":"வெண்ணீறு","parts":[{"text":"வெண்ணீறு","lemma":"veṇṇīṟu","gloss":"white ash"}],"gloss":"white ash"},{"surface":"அவிப்ப","parts":[{"text":"அவிப்ப","lemma":"avi","gloss":"to extinguish"}],"gloss":"to extinguish"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"எல்லார்","parts":[{"text":"எல்லார்","lemma":"ellār","gloss":"of all people"}],"gloss":"of all people"},{"surface":"புறனும்","parts":[{"text":"புறன்","lemma":"puṟaṉ","gloss":"the back"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and the end"},{"surface":"தான்","parts":[{"text":"தான்","lemma":"tāṉ","gloss":"itself"}],"gloss":"itself"},{"surface":"கண்டு","parts":[{"text":"கண்டு","lemma":"kāṇ","gloss":"having seen"}],"gloss":"having seen"},{"surface":"உலகத்து","parts":[{"text":"உலகத்து","lemma":"ulakam","gloss":"of the world"}],"gloss":"of the world"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மன்பதைக்கெல்லாம்","parts":[{"text":"மன்பதைக்கு","lemma":"maṉpatai","gloss":"to mankind"},{"text":"எல்லாம்","lemma":"ellām","gloss":"all"}],"gloss":"to all of mankind"},{"surface":"தானாய்","parts":[{"text":"தான்","lemma":"tāṉ","gloss":"itself"},{"text":"ஆய்","lemma":"āy","gloss":"having become"}],"gloss":"having become itself"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தன்புறம்","parts":[{"text":"தன்புறம்","lemma":"தன்புறம்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"காண்போர்க்","parts":[{"text":"காண்போர்க்","lemma":"காண்போர்க்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"காண்புஅறி","parts":[{"text":"காண்புஅறி","lemma":"காண்புஅறி","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"யாதே","parts":[{"text":"யாதே","lemma":"யாதே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true}],"literal":"Saline wasteland having spread, spurge cactus having grown high, / even in daytime hooting, with the horned owl of protruding teeth, / by the light of the funeral pyre, along with demoness women, / fear-inducing indeed is this mist-covered ancient crematorium, / where tears wept by heart-desiring lovers / extinguish the white ash of the bone-filled cremation ground; / having seen the end of everyone in this world, / having become everything to all of mankind, / it does not know anyone seeing its own end.","translation":"The saline wasteland has spread wide, and spurge cactus has grown high. Even in the daytime, horned owls with protruding teeth hoot. By the light of the funeral pyre, along with demoness women, this mist-shrouded ancient crematorium is indeed terrifying. Here, the tears wept by beloved partners extinguish the white ash of the bone-filled cremation ground. This place, which has seen the end of everyone in this world and has become the final destination for all of mankind, never knows anyone who can see its own end.","modern":"களர்நிலம் பரவி, கள்ளிச்செடிகள் வளர்ந்து, பகலிலும் அலறும் கூகையோடு, கோரப்பற்களை உடைய பேய்மகளிருடன், ஈமவிளக்கின் ஒளியில் விளங்கும் இந்த மேகம் சூழ்ந்த சுடுகாடு அச்சம் தருவதாகும். நெஞ்சில் நிறைந்த காதலர் அழுத கண்ணீர், எலும்புகள் நிறைந்த சுடுகாட்டின் வெண்ணீற்றை அணைக்கிறது. உலகத்து மக்கள் எல்லாரது முடிவையும் தான் கண்டு, மனிதகுலத்திற்கு எல்லாம் தானேயாகி நிற்கும் இந்தச் சுடுகாடு, தன் முடிவைக் காண்பாரை என்றுமே கண்டதில்லை.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Kāñci tiṇai (transience of life) and Peruṅkāñci tuṟai. The poet Tāyaṅkaṇṇaṉār describes the terrifying nature of the ancient crematorium (mutukāṭu) to emphasize the fleeting nature of human existence. He paints a vivid picture of a desolate wasteland overgrown with cactus, where owls hoot even during the day, and ghoulish women gather around the light of funeral pyres. The emotional core of the poem is the image of grieving lovers whose tears extinguish the hot ashes of the pyre. Ultimately, the poet personifies the crematorium as an eternal entity that witnesses the end of every human being, yet remains immortal itself, as no one can ever witness its demise.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}